            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Described herein is a method of providing a hydrocarbon polymer from a hydrocarbon mixture, the hydrocarbon mixture comprising a cyclic olefin. The method comprises: contacting the hydrocarbon mixture with a 10-ring pore molecular sieve at a temperature of -20°C to 60 °C for a time and under conditions to provide a sieved hydrocarbon mixture comprising the cyclic olefin; contacting the sieved hydrocarbon mixture with a polymerization catalyst for a time and under conditions to polymerize the cyclic olefin, thereby forming the hydrocarbon polymer. The 10-ring pore molecular sieve has a sieving channel with a 10-ring sieving aperture with a minimum crystallographic free diameter greater than 3Å and a ratio of the maximum crystallographic free diameter to the minimum crystallographic free diameter between 1 and 2; a T1/T2 ratio ≥ 20:1, wherein T1 is an element independently selected from Si, Ge and a combination thereof, and T2 is an element independently selected from Al, B, Ga and a combination thereof; and a counterion selected from NH4&lt;+>, Li&lt;+>, Na&lt;+>, K&lt;+>, Ca&lt;2+> and a combination thereof. Also described is a hydrocarbon polymer obtained by the method.</p>
            </abstract>
